  "body": "Closes #13694 (and #8970, whose last open criterion this closes).\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilds the mux consumer of the serve-proxy credit primitive (design record #5792): a new `Mux` in `pkgs/id/src/serve_proxy_mux.rs` holding a per-stream `CreditWindow` per open stream plus one aggregate per-connection window.\n\n- **DATA-accept path:** `accept_data` admits a payload only when both the stream window and the aggregate connection window cover it, consuming both atomically; a refusal changes neither window, so credit is never exceeded and never goes negative.\n- **Credit-return path:** `apply_window_update` grants a received WINDOW_UPDATE to the named stream window (or the connection window for stream 0), bounded by each window's ceiling. An over-ceiling or overflowing grant is rejected with an ERROR frame carrying `ErrorReason::CreditOverrun` and leaves the window unchanged — never silently saturated (#8970). A WINDOW_UPDATE for an unknown stream (or a non-WINDOW_UPDATE frame) maps to a `ProtocolViolation` ERROR frame.\n- **Credit returns only as bounded buffer space is released:** closing a stream drops its stream window and does not refund connection credit — that credit returns only via a connection WINDOW_UPDATE from the peer (HTTP/2-style). Ceilings stay parameterized from the effective configuration (`Mux::with_credit`); no universal deployment limit is invented.\n- Tests: 9 unit tests + 1 model property test (`mux_accounting_matches_the_model`) over interleaved opens/accepts/grants/closes, naming #13694/#8970 as oracle.\n\nThis branch also carries a blocker fix (separate commit): commit 819e0f455 added the `at: Option<u64>` field to `id_events::groups::Event` without updating five struct literals in the `id` crate's test fixtures, so `cargo test -p id --lib` failed to compile on main (E0063). The fixtures predate timestamps, so `at: None` is the documented-correct value. Current main still carries the break; this PR fixes it in passing.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRemote verification via the `fleet-command.yml` workflow fallback (`fleet queue dispatch` is blocked by TLS defect #13185):\n\n- `cargo test -p id --lib serve_proxy_mux` on `xaltha/13694-credit-mux` @ `93f93be1d`: **10 passed, 0 failed** (589 filtered out) — run https://github.com/developing-today/fleet/actions/runs/45287417777 (conclusion: success).\n- Before the fix, the same command failed to compile on main's HEAD with 5× E0063 in `hosted_binding.rs`/`pull_policy.rs` (run 45284168795); after the `at: None` commit the lib test target compiles and the 10 mux tests run green.\n- Not built locally; relies on the remote run above. No new test file, so no suite-registry row is needed (inline tests in the already-registered `id.rust.unit` target).\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n- New module only, plus one `pub mod` line in `pkgs/id/src/lib.rs` and five `at: None` lines in test fixtures. No behaviour change outside the new mux and the previously uncompilable test fixtures.\n- The mux is not yet wired into any live leg (leg establishment is a later slice on #7569); nothing calls `Mux` yet, so this cannot change runtime behaviour.\n- Branch merges cleanly against current main (verified with `git merge-tree`, no conflicts).\n\n<!-- pm-metadata:start -->\n```json\n{\n  \"direct_parent\": null,\n  \"links\": [],\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"design\": null,\n    \"roadmap_item\": null,\n    \"priority\": null\n  },\n  \"pm_meta\": 1,\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"queue_id\": null,\n    \"scheduled_start\": null,\n    \"picked_up_at\": null,\n    \"work_started_at\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-11-23T23:37:31Z\",\n    \"session_id\": null,\n    \"lane\": null,\n    \"host\": \"htch-runtime\",\n    \"worktree\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/github-work/code-13694-credit-mux\",\n    \"model\": null,\n    \"lane_start_issues\": [],\n    \"workspace_ref\": {\n      \"kind\": \"worktree\",\n      \"id\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/github-work/code-13694-credit-mux\",\n      \"repo\": \"developing-today/code\",\n      \"branch\": \"xaltha/13694-credit-mux\",\n      \"sha\": \"93f93be1dffd658c6686f216879830d56a9c5ecc\"\n    },\n    \"auth_subject\": \"xaltha\",\n    \"stamped_by\": \"fleet 0.1.0 (native)\"\n  }\n}\n```\n<!-- pm-metadata:end -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://dashboardbackend.blacksmith.sh/track/run-proof?expires=1798069058&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=13859&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F13859&variant=proof_this_pr&signature=7bb0e50ab77c168fed6886685a7c1fc3fefe57cf899c3f8b24bc84358e7915fe\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Proof this PR\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/proof-proof-this-pr-v2-dark-3x.png\" width=\"121\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/13859?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
